  "note": "Bare primitive arguments are type-checked at the command boundary (C3.8): a fractional Integer, a string Float, and a list String are each TypeMismatch refusals before any rule runs, never faults. A boolean argument (declared `TrueClass`) offered a map or a list is refused the same way. The well-formed Measure before and after them is accepted. The Ruby-only String-admits-an-integer asymmetry is deliberately not exercised.",
